=== SURVEY ===
Web source ChartExportMenu.tsx = a single Download-icon ghost-button trigger that toggles an
absolute-positioned `role="menu"` of export actions, closing on outside-click / Escape:
  • "Download data as CSV"   (chart.export.csv)   — optional lead item, present only when
                                                     `onExportCsv` is supplied; ignores `busy`.
  • "Save as PNG"            (chart.export.png)   — disabled while `busy` (snapshot in flight).
  • "Save as SVG"            (chart.export.svg)   — disabled while `busy`.
  • "Copy image to clipboard"(chart.export.copy)  — disabled while `busy`; awaits onCopyImage()
                                                     → ClipboardOutcome ('copied'|'fallback'|
                                                     'failed') → toast success/info/error.
The trigger's aria-label switches disabled→"Chart not ready to export"(disabledTooltip) /
enabled→"Export chart"(menuLabel); `disabled` prevents the menu opening. It degrades gracefully
without a ToastProvider because `useOptionalToast()` returns null (web `if (!toast) return`).
Data sources (P1/S8): useTranslation (P1/S10 facade), useOptionalToast (optional toast seam) —
NO network and NO data-fetch state holder. Shared components: ui/Button, feedback/Toast.
Charts/maps: none. Canonical props-driven sibling studied: shared-surfaces/AiOutputPanel (the only
web hook is useTranslation; "there is no data source to bind, only the localisation facade and the
render maths"); native Menu idiom studied: feature-views/InboxBody.RowMenu.

=== REASONING ===
- The native surface reproduces the web composition with SwiftUI's `Menu` — the HIG-idiomatic
  counterpart to the hand-rolled web popover: it provides the pop-up-button trait, keyboard
  activation, and outside-tap / Escape dismissal for free, so the web open-state plumbing
  (useEffect mousedown/keydown listeners) is not ported — the platform owns it. The trigger label
  is a muted Download SF Symbol (ghost-icon parity); each row is a `Button { Label { Text } icon:
  { Image(systemName:) } }` mirroring a web `role="menuitem"`.
- Architecture mirrors the props-driven AiOutputPanel leaf (no Adapter/Projection/Seams files
  because there is genuinely no data source — only the localisation facade + an optional toast):
  • Model (Foundation/Observation/OSLog): ChartExportClipboardOutcome (web ClipboardOutcome),
    ChartExportMenuAction (csv/png/svg/copy, dependsOnSnapshot), ChartExportToastSeverity/Intent,
    ChartExportMenuItem; ChartExportMenuLogic (pure projection — menuItems(hasCsv:busy:), the
    trigger-label switch, canOpen, the clipboard-outcome → toast mapping); ChartExportMenuMeta
    (slug); ChartExportMenuTelemetry seam (P1/S11 view.opened) + OSLog default + Diagnostics seam;
    ChartExportMenuToastPresenter (the native useOptionalToast — @MainActor AnyObject, optional);
    ChartExportMenuStrings (P1/S10 facade); @MainActor @Observable ChartExportMenuModel (owns the
    host export callbacks + optional toast; perform()/exportPNG()/exportSVG()/copyImage();
    markAppeared() emits view.opened once).
  • swift (the View): Menu trigger bound through the model; designated + closure-wiring inits.
  • Views: the Download trigger label + the per-row menu item button.
  • Previews: default(+CSV) / without-CSV / disabled / busy / copy-demo(toast wired).
  • strings: the exact 9 web keys; Tests + ModelTests.
- "Every web branch renders" honoured for the control's REAL branches (this is a props-driven menu,
  not a data surface — the generic loading/empty/error/stale/offline template states do not exist
  in the web source; faithful parity = reproducing the branches that DO exist, per the AiOutputPanel
  precedent which documented the same for its single non-data hook):
    disabled (trigger inert + label switch), busy (PNG/SVG/Copy disabled, CSV unaffected), CSV
    present vs absent, and the three copy outcomes (copied→success / fallback→info / failed→error,
    plus the no-presenter graceful-degrade).
- Side effects off the view: the async onCopyImage/onExportPNG/onExportSVG and the toast
  announcement live on the @MainActor model so no `Task`-sending / Sendable plumbing leaks into the
  SwiftUI layer (the project builds under SWIFT_STRICT_CONCURRENCY=complete / Swift 6 language mode).
- Rejected: porting the web outside-click/Escape useEffect (SwiftUI Menu handles dismissal);
  porting Tailwind classes / raw hex (used P1/S9 tokens); a synchronous copy (web awaits the
  Promise<ClipboardOutcome> — modelled as `@MainActor () async -> ChartExportClipboardOutcome`);
  hiding the CSV item's enablement behind `busy` (web CSV ignores busy — asserted).

